8460001-8909c987-b9ee-4b19-b213-b298908296ae"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"492d9899d207219a410c08444926e06a0cd1771a8e3f28c206be55112bfd9e6a","event_uuid":"afc1e79d-e98d-411f-b98a-c103c6e2809d","position":{"commit_sha":"09d9d824e7719f7d1406c60db89253df750cb4d5","position":"1787569586515902001-afc1e79d-e98d-411f-b98a-c103c6e2809d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"1c3e3b6256a7d2a2e7c50aca727b15c8367ebb12ff60dd2c3e39d5d8647c6ad4","event_uuid":"0d9831ef-0502-424d-8ed9-6e21879e1b8f","position":{"commit_sha":"c729894d58a1a20c7dc4fd36e45d6cfcb924f9cc","position":"1787569605474874001-0d9831ef-0502-424d-8ed9-6e21879e1b8f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented under RED->GREEN TDD. Decision recorded: retain primary-only pack scope, add a pack-layer `complete` boolean (false only when alternates present) so an alternates-backed shared clone is explicitly non-exclusive and cannot be read as the whole object store; linked-worktree pack stays complete. Portable-test gaps closed: allocation asserted from injected st_blocks (no filesystem block-policy dependence), plus direct tests for allocation-unavailable text and CLI bad-argument exit 2. schema requires pack.complete; user-guide/reuse-surface updated. make lint + make typecheck GREEN; 47 focused footprint/schema tests + 71 help/reference/registry tests GREEN (with harness GIT_CONFIG safe.bareRepository env cleared for the pre-existing bare-repo interface test, which is environmental and passes on CI). Pushed Gerrit change 2183; awaiting LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1.","timestamp":1787563003092103001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787544613312234001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"fb6d0122-5ff0-43b3-ae3f-28965674eae9","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"0754-cfc5-e451-4e9b"},{"link_uuid":"f6e1cfe8-b9c5-4c34-bb3d-420deb575d95","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"f416-2494-7791-4c09"},{"link_uuid":"99fb6f13-4e7f-4fe3-9f95-686d02fd728d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"e23c-0415-4d9f-4a46"},{"link_uuid":"41bc13db-9c0e-4352-b98c-1e2edf6a4d35","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"28a4-d486-d74e-4d36"}],"description":"## Context\n\nGerrit change 2169 (parent task 0754-cfc5-e451-4e9b) added the explicit, opt-in, read-only\n`rebar tracker-footprint` command. LLM review recorded four non-blocking hardening\nopportunities. This task addresses them without changing the command's opt-in, read-only,\nunscheduled, non-gating, threshold-free contract.\n\nFindings:\n1. Correctness/misuse: the mounted `pack` layer measures only the primary common Git object\n   database (`objects/pack/*.pack`). An alternates-backed shared clone (`git clone --shared`)\n   keeps its objects in the borrowed alternate object database, so the primary pack layer can\n   report near-zero. The report already labels the object database `shared`, but a reader can\n   still mistake the small `pack.logical_bytes` for an exclusive/complete whole-object-store\n   measurement.\n2. Portability: an interface assertion (`checkout_allocated > pack_logical * 4`) assumes each\n   one-byte file is charged a full filesystem block; this fails on block-suballocating /\n   tail-packing filesystems.\n3. The allocation-unavailable text rendering path has no direct test.\n4. The CLI bad-argument (argparse) exit-2 path has no direct test.\n\n## Decision (recorded)\n\nRetain **primary-only** pack scope rather than enumerating alternate object databases.\nEnumerating alternates would count borrowed, shared objects as this clone's local footprint\nand contradict the established whole-clone inode-dedup philosophy (shared bytes are not this\nclone's cost). Instead make the primary-only measurement **explicitly non-exclusive**: add a\n`complete` boolean to the `pack` layer — `true` when the measured `.pack` files are the\ncomplete object store backing this checkout, `false` when the checkout borrows objects from an\nunmeasured alternate object database (`\"alternates\"` present in `shared_reasons`). A linked\nworktree's pack is measured from the common dir and remains `complete: true` (shared across\nworktrees but complete). The `pack` definition string is updated to state this, and the text\nrenderer surfaces `complete` with a clarifying note when false.\n\n## Plan\n\n- footprint.py: `_pack_layer` gains `complete: bool`; `measure_tracker` computes\n  `complete = \"alternates\" not in reasons`. Update `DEFINITIONS[\"pack\"]` to describe the\n  primary-only, non-exclusive semantics.\n- schema: add required `complete` boolean to `pack_layer`.\n- tracker_footprint.py `_render_text`: render `complete=…` for the pack layer, with a\n  parenthetical when non-exclusive.\n- Tests (RED→GREEN):\n  - Unit: standalone and linked-worktree pack `complete: true`; alternates pack `complete:\n    false`.\n  - Unit: injected-`st_blocks` assertion proves allocation = Σ(st_blocks·512) deterministically\n    (replaces the filesystem-ratio assumption).\n  - Unit (new tests/unit/commands/test_tracker_footprint.py): `_render_text` renders the\n    allocation-unavailable label.\n  - Interface: replace the `* 4` ratio with portable assertions (allocation available, small\n    file count, pack complete/standalone, pack>0); add a bad-argument exit-2 CLI test.\n- docs/user-guide.md, docs/reuse-surface.md: document the pack `complete` field.\n- Preserve opt-in, read-only, unscheduled, non-gating, threshold-free behavior.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] The `pack` layer carries a `complete` boolean; an alternates-backed mounted clone reports\n      `complete: false` so it cannot be mistaken for an exclusive whole-object-store pack\n      measurement; standalone and linked-worktree report `complete: true`. (unit + schema)\n- [x] A real `git clone --shared` fixture proves the alternates ownership/dedup semantics\n      without double-counting shared objects. (unit)\n- [x] Allocation-unavailable text rendering and CLI bad-argument exit 2 have direct tests.\n- [x] Allocation assertions use injected/stat capability rather than a filesystem block policy.\n- [x] The command stays opt-in, read-only, unscheduled, non-gating, and threshold-free.\n- [x] make lint, make typecheck, and focused tests pass; generated help/reference stay green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/footprint.py","reason":"Add pack-layer complete flag and non-exclusive primary-only semantics"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/tracker_footprint.py","reason":"Render pack complete flag with non-exclusive note in text output"},{"path":"src/rebar/schemas/tracker_footprint.schema.json","reason":"Require complete boolean on pack_layer"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_footprint.py","reason":"Cover pack complete flag, alternates incompleteness, injected-st_blocks allocation"},{"path":"tests/unit/commands/test_tracker_footprint.py","reason":"New: direct test of allocation-unavailable text rendering"},{"path":"tests/interfaces/test_tracker_footprint_cli.py","reason":"Replace filesystem-ratio assertion; add bad-argument exit-2 test"},{"path":"docs/user-guide.md","reason":"Document pack complete field / non-exclusive semantics"},{"path":"docs/reuse-surface.md","reason":"Document pack complete field on measure_tracker output"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","28a4-d486-d74e-4d36"],["relates_to","e23c-0415-4d9f-4a46"],["relates_to","f416-2494-7791-4c09"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"afc1e79d-e98d-411f-b98a-c103c6e2809d","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["footprint","git","tests"],"ticket_id":"ed53-bc12-ab39-4845","ticket_type":"task","title":"Harden tracker-footprint shared-clone semantics and edge-path coverage","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b833295f-ce49-493a-85c7-5b8ee6963129","39c2480b-da35-4234-827c-4d97242a54bf","98ac4a15-2a9c-4b34-932e-d9f24acc6ba5","2f1c4d1e-ab0d-466e-8c65-dac7c182e644","f963b509-d1ed-472b-b819-c6c23e7c0e42","e0d695f9-1fd3-4ca6-8cb4-31ba32938c9a","f6e1cfe8-b9c5-4c34-bb3d-420deb575d95","99fb6f13-4e7f-4fe3-9f95-686d02fd728d","41bc13db-9c0e-4352-b98c-1e2edf6a4d35","8909c987-b9ee-4b19-b213-b298908296ae","afc1e79d-e98d-411f-b98a-c103c6e2809d","0d9831ef-0502-424d-8ed9-6e21879e1b8f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787572805082027001,"uuid":"11dc39e1-2433-4309-b3d8-7e9aff435bff"}